{"seq": 131, "at": "2026-11-09T20:18:25Z", "issue": 167, "action": "update_view", "actor": "pendragon.avalon", "owner": "arthur", "entity": "ideas/miax-options-volume/views/pendragon.avalon", "version": 2, "target_date": "2027-12-09", "proposal_sha256": "045ce96b0d7ae162d004ca90bc845a530c744fc57ba54d00bf669d02f1a12225", "diff": {"horizon_months": [14, 13], "target_date": ["2027-12-25", "2027-12-09"], "derived.expected_price": [44.238, 45.638], "derived.expected_return": [0.301883, 0.290485], "derived.p10": [21.09, 21.9], "derived.p50": [43.49, 44.95], "derived.p90": [62.16, 62.78]}, "rationale": "Version 2, after the third-quarter 2026 results: still standing aside, with the distribution moved up. The results came on 29 October 2026, not in early November as v1 stated. Against the four tests we set in v1: net transaction revenue rose 14% year over year and the quarterly options market share was 17.4%, above both the 16% and the 15.5% thresholds; access fees grew 36% and market data fees 29%, far from single digits; the diluted share count rose 0.1% on the second quarter, well under 1%; and net cash rose to about $697 million, none of it spent on buybacks or acquisitions. In v1 we wrote that if transaction revenue kept growing after the volatility peak, market share stayed above 16% and the share count stopped rising, the case would rest on more than our forecast; all three happened, so we put less weight on the conservative case and the middle of the distribution is higher. We do not change the position. Excalibur keeps a company only when its discount is a framing error that can be corrected. The quarter made the business look healthier, but the remaining discount still reflects earnings that move with options volume and the fee per contract: revenue per contract fell 4.9% year over year as market share rose, and October volume was 13.5% below a very strong October 2025 (c2 unmet). The engine still fails the uniqueness test (c1 partial), and incentives are still not tied to the share price (c4 unmet). Other changes, several of them suggested by Caspar.Magi's review of v1: the September and October 2026 monthly trading reports, the 2026 proxy statement and the three Form 4 filings on the only open-market purchases are recorded as evidence; the process notes write out how we compute the share of transaction revenue and which market-share series the thresholds use; we explain why we keep the left tail thin; we judge adjusted EBITDA on the definition used until the second quarter; and the horizon is 13 months so that the target date stays close to 31 December 2027. As in v1, we disclose the distribution and the method that produces it, not the scenario values, probabilities or valuation multiples. The next tests are the fourth-quarter 2026 results, expected in February 2027, and the monthly reports before them.", "discussion_refs": ["https://github.com/the-magi-system/magi/issues/56#issuecomment-6396626630", "https://github.com/the-magi-system/magi/issues/56#issuecomment-6396817797"]}
